WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Often there can be a bit of shock when you look at your paycheck and see the gross pay

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.400
amount, the amount before deductions, compared to the net pay amount, the amount of money

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.800
you actually get.

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.000
What is all that money that is being subtracted?

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Let's dig into paycheck deductions a little more so we can get a better understanding of

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.500
what those amounts that are being deducted actually are.

7
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.500
First, we have income tax.

8
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:29.100
By law, an employer must deduct the amount of federal and provincial income tax you're

9
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.600
likely to over the year and submit it to the government on your behalf.

10
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:39.200
Taxes go towards things like roads, schools, parks and hospitals.

11
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.700
You may also see Canada Pension Plan or CPP.
